Package: com.lettherotconsumeapple-rootless
Name: Rotten Apple
Version: 0.0.1
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: This tweak was MEANT to disable your daemon permanently, whether you like it or not, after installing it'll make the plist persistent despite being in stock iOS.                                                                           Yes this means it is significantly giving you more risk of bootlooping even when you're using rootless, so be careful with what you're disabling.                                                                                    More technical details, this tweak modifies the existing /var/db/com.apple.xpc.launchd/disabled.501.plist and it simply just changes the chmod permission with 0644 to prevent the existing disabled list from getting rewritten by iOS.                                                                             This tweak is simply isn't an exploit as you still need to disable the daemon yourself with third party app (iCleaner Pro) or 'launchctl' command although I hadn't tested that command, those things still need root privileges access like jailbreaking, rootless is only limited to /var so theres that.                                          If you want to revert everything back, just uninstall the tweak and reboot userspace then you're good to go.
Maintainer: pawxed
Author: pawxed
Section: System
Depends: mobilesubstrate

